  "term": "WMS",
  "definition": "WMS, or Wyburn-Mason syndrome, is a rare condition present from birth that is not inherited. It involves multiple, often large abnormal connections between arteries and veins, mainly affecting the retina, brain, eye socket, and facial tissues.",
